\[
\begin{cases}
20x + y = 2197 \\
y = \sqrt[3]{20x + 13}
\end{cases}
\]
Substituting $y = \sqrt[3]{20x + 13}$ into the first equation, we get $20x + \sqrt[3]{20x + 13} = 2197$. By letting $z = \sqrt[3]{20x + 13}$, we have $20x = z^3 - 13$ and $20x + z = 2197$. Thus, $z^3 - 13 + z = 2197$, which simplifies to $z^3 + z - 2210 = 0$. We solve this equation for $z$. By trial and error or using numerical methods, we find that $z = 12$ is a solution. Substituting $z = 12$ back into the equation, we get $12^3 + 12 - 2210 = 1728 + 12 - 2210 = 0$, which confirms that $z = 12$ is indeed a solution. Now we can find $x$: $20x + 12 = 2197 \Rightarrow 20x = 2185 \Rightarrow x = \frac{2185}{20} = 109.25$.
